    I("What is an element?",
      "An **element** is a substance that **cannot be broken down** into simpler substances by chemical reactions. Hydrogen and oxygen are elements; water is not.",
      then=["About 90 elements occur naturally, and everything around us is made of them. Hydrogen is the most common element in the Universe; oxygen is the most common in the Earth's crust and in your body."]),
    I("Chemical symbols",
      "Every element has a **chemical symbol** – the same in every language. The first letter is always a **capital**; a second letter is always **small**.",
      table=[["From the English name", "", "From the Latin name", ""],
             ["H", "hydrogen", "Na", "sodium (natrium)"], ["C", "carbon", "K", "potassium (kalium)"], ["O", "oxygen", "Fe", "iron (ferrum)"],
             ["Mg", "magnesium", "Cu", "copper (cuprum)"], ["Cl", "chlorine", "Ag", "silver (argentum)"], ["He", "helium", "Pb", "lead (plumbum)"]],
      then=["Watch the capitals: **Co** is cobalt, but **CO** is carbon monoxide – two elements joined."]),
